Z||000000||Philphine||08-25-2001||10:19 PM||||<BR>if you had already decided to go with a 4:10 tranny, what engine or engines would you match up with it if fun and/or performance (within financial/practicle reason. i don't mean a twin turbo northstar or the like) were the main goals? i'm guessing a high revver.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||08-25-2001||10:45 PM||||3.4 Twin Dual Cam.  With mods, it'll rev like crazy and makes great power, too.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||08-25-2001||11:18 PM||||Does the 4:10 have the .73 or the .81 for 4th? I've heard both, but i know one of those ratios are right and the other is from the economy 4 spd.<P>The engine choice depends on how you plan to use the car. If it's just a weekend cruiser, go for a high revving small block. If you want to drive it alot more, go with a high revving 6. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||jelly2m8||08-25-2001||11:21 PM||||Yep, get a screamer. I spun a rod bearing in the first 350 I put in my V8. Had the 4.10 in it, and didnt have the tach mod then. Was runnin with the speedo needle straight down ( 85mph speedo), then knock knock knock...woops!<P> Even with a motor that will turn 7k, dont expect much more speed than 135 mph or so||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||08-26-2001||12:08 PM||||What about putting a 4:10 final drive in a 5 speed tranny? This can be done, can't it?<P>I honestly don't want to take my Indy anywhere out of town because of the slow speeds with the 4:10...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||EdsB52||08-26-2001||12:45 PM||||Other than drag racing, the 4:10 is a boat anchor. I gave one away a couple months ago and have another one I'm probably going to give away. I'm thinking about buying a fishing boat so I may keep it. Even with a 3.4TDC I think the 4:10 is geared too short. It's like a jap bike tranny (rato wise).||||reg||1
